{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794769666,"nonce":"Qyr3akkaflqYU0XVaXkDlMO2yHk=","message":"c63ad70d: found by hxn: a primitive an archive defines (hlp_future_state, from @:hlNative(\"counter\") field future_state) was silently replaced by the runtime's hlp_future_state (std/src/future.rs). HashLink gives each .hdll its own namespace; a wasm link has one, and 'the earlier definition wins' sent the program's call to the wrong function (unthreaded it trapped with an indirect call type mismatch, threaded it hung). The link now fails when a shadowed entry is one the program binds to a library, naming both definitions. Not done: resolving the primitive inside its own archive, which needs each native's (lib, name) mapped to the archive that provides the library; hxn renamed its fixture's primitives instead. Separate regression of mine, fixed in the same commit: c76c3e0b used ash_wasm_link, an optional dependency, outside the llvm feature, so ash_core no longer built without it (ash_nair_hl). I had only checked with default features.","files":null}]}